+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `payhook/config.py`: `read_dotenv` now strips a leading `export `, removes matching single or double quotes around values, splits on the first `=` only (so values containing `=` work), and skips lines without `=`. Added `SECRETS` and `mask()`.
+- `payhook/__main__.py`: new `python -m payhook doctor`. It prints `KEY = value  [env|.env|default]` for every setting, and `(not set)` for unset ones.
+- Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are **masked** to `****` plus the last 4 characters, so the output is safe to paste into a ticket.
+- `README.md`: documented `doctor`.
+- `tests/test_doctor_mask.py`: new test for masking and source labels. No existing tests were touched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: 5 tests, all OK. That is the 4 existing tests (including the quoted, `export` and `=`-in-value cases and the existing doctor test) plus the new one.
+- `python -m payhook doctor` in the repo, against the real `.env`: the export-prefixed `PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` loaded with its `=` and `&` intact, and sources showed `.env` or `default` correctly. Secrets were masked.
+- `.env` is unmodified and still git-ignored (`git status --ignored` shows `!! .env`).
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not test an environment-variable value that overrides `.env` through the CLI. The existing unit test covers it at the `load_config` level.
+- The loader does not handle escape sequences inside double quotes, inline `# comments` after values, or multi-line values.
+- **Needs your decision:** `docs/SUPPORT.md` (outside the files I may edit) tells support the pasted configuration must include the full API key. I did not implement that, because `doctor` output is meant to go into tickets. If support needs to identify an account, the last 4 characters may do. Otherwise, add an explicit opt-in flag. That doc also still refers to `check`, and should probably point at `doctor` and drop the full-key advice.
